We are looking for a collaborative and people-oriented Scrum Master to support our Connectivity Verification teams.
In this role, you will help software development and test automation teams work effectively in an Agile environment. You will facilitate the Scrum process, support the teams in removing impediments, and encourage continuous improvement while contributing to innovative solutions that improve the lives of people with hearing loss.
Working with us, You will receive:
full-time employment in an international organization;
learning and development opportunities adapted to your needs and supporting your growth;
hybrid work model with in Mierzyn office;
flexible working hours;
Scandinavian culture – informal, focused on equality, independence, open dialogue, and work-life balance;
opportunity to work with highly skilled Agile teams developing cutting-edge Bluetooth and connectivity technology for hearing aids;
opportunity to develop your Agile and SAFe knowledge while supporting continuous improvement;
benefits package including private medical care, insurance, sport card, and other social benefits.
What tasks are waiting for you?
Support Scrum teams as a servant leader, helping them work effectively and continuously improve.
Facilitate Agile ceremonies, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, reviews, and retrospectives.
Support Product Owners and teams with backlog refinement and sprint planning.
Help the teams identify and remove impediments that affect their progress.
Encourage effective collaboration and communication within the teams and with stakeholders.
Promote Agile principles and support the teams in delivering high-quality incremental value.
Track basic team metrics and help teams monitor their progress toward sprint and PI objectives.
Participate in PI Planning and support collaboration with other teams within the Agile Release Train.
Work with other Scrum Masters and relevant stakeholders to address dependencies and challenges.
Support the teams in experimenting, learning, and continuously improving their ways of working.
Help create an environment where team members feel empowered to take ownership and contribute their ideas.
Apply today if you:
have 2+ years of experience as a Scrum Master or in a similar Agile role;
have a good understanding of Agile principles and Scrum; experience with Kanban is a plus;
have an interest in SAFe or some experience working in a SAFe environment;
have good facilitation, communication, and collaboration skills;
are comfortable working with cross-functional teams and different stakeholders;
are able to identify problems, facilitate discussions, and help teams find solutions;
have experience working with software development or test automation teams;
are fluent in English, both spoken and written.
It would be nice if you:
have experience with eg. Jira, Confluence, Miro, Power BI, or similar tools;
have experience working in a SAFe environment;
are familiar with Lean principles and continuous delivery;
have experience working with software testing or test automation;
hold a Scrum Master or Agile certification.
Please send your English CV!

