Choosing Capgemini means choosing a company where you will be empowered to shape your career in the way you’d like, where you’ll be supported and inspired by a collaborative community of colleagues around the world, and where you’ll be able to reimagine what’s possible. Join us and help the world’s leading organizations unlock the value of technology and build a more sustainable, more inclusive world.
Your role
Become a part of a team of over 300 SAP specialists. We combine deep technological expertise with strategic business consulting, delivering innovative solutions to global enterprises, including Fortune 500 companies. Working across diverse industries, we support our clients in achieving their business transformation goals.
Your tasks
lead SAP APO implementations, enhancements, upgrades, and production support activities across supply chain planning functions;
configure and support APO modules including: Demand Planning (DP), Integrated Demand Planning (IDP), Distribution Requirements Planning (DRP), Supply Network Planning (SNP), Production Planning & Detailed Scheduling (PP/DS), Global Available-to-Promise (GATP);
serve as the functional Subject Matter Expert for SAP APO planning capabilities and related supply chain applications;
support end-to-end Price Repository (PR) business processes, integrations, planning data management activities and Rulex application functionality, business processes, and system integrations;
lead and support Cannibalizer analysis, including demand shaping, product substitution analysis, forecast adjustments, promotional impacts, and inventory optimization initiatives;
support enterprise planning applications including APO IDP, APO DRP, Rulex, Price Repository (PR), Scrapp Application, and Cannibalizer solutions;
collaborate with business stakeholders to identify forecasting trends, demand drivers, and opportunities for process improvement;
support integration between SAP APO, SAP ECC, SAP S/4HANA, SAP IBP, SAP BW, databases, and related enterprise applications.
Your profile
8+ years of SAP Supply Chain experience with strong expertise in SAP APO planning solutions;
hands-on experience supporting Demand Planning (DP), Integrated Demand Planning (IDP), Distribution Requirements Planning (DRP), Supply Network Planning (SNP), Production Planning & Detailed Scheduling (PP/DS), Global Available-to-Promise (GATP);
strong understanding of end-to-end supply chain planning processes including forecasting, replenishment, inventory optimization, supply planning, and production scheduling;
proven experience supporting: End-to-end Price Repository (PR) application processes and integrations and End-to-end Rulex application functionality, administration, and business integration;
deep expertise in Cannibalizer analysis, demand shaping, promotional forecasting, forecast consumption, and product substitution modeling;
demonstrated ability to leverage cannibalization insights to improve forecast accuracy, inventory positioning, replenishment planning, and overall supply chain effectiveness;
experience supporting and managing enterprise planning systems including APO IDP, APO DRP, Rulex, Price Repository, Scrapp Application, and Cannibalizer solutions;
strong knowledge of planning data structures, forecasting methodologies, inventory optimization concepts, and planning analytics;
experience integrating SAP APO with SAP ECC, SAP S/4HANA, SAP BW, SAP IBP, and related supply chain applications;
exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to independently diagnose and resolve highly complex planning and forecasting challenges;
strong communication and stakeholder management skills with the ability to influence planning decisions and business outcomes.
Nice to have
SAP APO and SAP IBP Certification;
experience with SAP IBP Demand Planning, Supply Planning, Inventory Optimization, Response & Supply, and S&OP processes and supporting large-scale supply chain transformation and planning modernization initiatives;
working knowledge of SAP S/4HANA Supply Chain Planning capabilities;
experience with advanced forecasting models, statistical forecasting, and demand planning methodologies;
knowledge of ABAP debugging and technical troubleshooting;
experience with SAP BW, reporting solutions, Operational Data Stores (ODS), and planning data architecture.
What You'll love about working here?
Practical benefits: private medical care with Medicover with additional packages (e.g., dental, senior care, oncology) available on preferential terms, life insurance and 40+ options on our NAIS benefit platform, including Netflix, Spotify or Sports card.
Access to over 70 training tracks with certification opportunities (e.g., GenAI, Architects, Google) on our NEXT platform. Dive into a world of knowledge with free access to Education First languages platform, TED Talks and Udemy Business materials and trainings.
Enjoy hybrid working model that fits your life - after completing onboarding, connect work from a modern office with ergonomic work from home, thanks to home office package (including laptop, monitor, and chair). Ask your recruiter about the details.
Community Hub that will allow you to choose from over 20 professional communities that gather people interested in, among others: Salesforce, Java, Could, IoT, Agile, AI.
Get to know us
Capgemini is committed to diversity and inclusion, ensuring fairness in all employment practices. We evaluate individuals based on qualifications and performance, not personal characteristics, striving to create a workplace where everyone can succeed and feel valued.
Do you want to get to know us better? Check our Instagram — @capgeminipl or visit our Facebook profile — Capgemini Polska. You can also find us on YouTube.
Capgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner, delivering tangible business value. We imagine the future of organizations and make it real with AI, technology and people. With our strong heritage of nearly 60 years, we are a responsible and diverse group of 420,000 team members in more than 50 countries. We deliver end-to-end services and solutions with our deep industry expertise and strong partner ecosystem, leveraging our capabilities across strategy, technology, design, engineering and business operations. The Group reported 2024 global revenues of €22.1 billion.
