We are searching for candidates for a senior Oracle DBA role focused on performance optimization, resource efficiency and project delivery across Oracle ExaCC (Exadata Cloud@Customer), ZFS and ZDLRA environments. Day-to-day operational coverage is handled in partnership with infrastructure teams; this role focuses on specialist expertise, continuous improvement and cross-team collaboration with development and infrastructure stakeholders.
What You'll Do
Optimize Oracle database performance through compression techniques, query tuning and indexing strategy — with a focus on ExaCC CPU efficiency, storage cost reduction and I/O efficiency;
Fine-tune Oracle CPU allocation algorithms on ExaCC to maximize the used/allocated ratio and minimize waste;
Optimize backup and recovery processes for Oracle ZFS and ZDLRA appliances, ensuring reliability and cost-effectiveness;
Lead and support key projects, including migration to Kerberos authentication and Oracle Client upgrades;
Guide development teams on best practices for database design, SQL coding, performance and scalability;
Perform root cause analysis on performance incidents and complex database issues escalated from infrastructure partners;
Enforce access management, TDE encryption, auditing controls and audit-quality documentation;
Contribute to multi-platform environments (Azure SQL, PostgreSQL, Synapse) where relevant;
Collaborate with infrastructure partners, development teams and project stakeholders across initiatives.
What You'll Need
Qualifications
University degree in Computer Science, Engineering or comparable technical field;
5-10 years of hands-on experience with Oracle databases in production environments;
Proven expertise in performance tuning, compression and resource optimization;
Hands-on experience with ExaCC, ZFS and ZDLRA is a strong plus;
OS knowledge: Linux and/or Unix (primary), Windows (secondary).
